---
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

const weeks = [
  {
    n: "01",
    name: "Week one",
    body: "We go through what you're trying to build, who it's for, what already exists, and what you're constrained by. Most of this is us asking questions and you correcting our answers.",
  },
  {
    n: "02",
    name: "Week two",
    body: "We turn that into decisions: what's in the first version, what isn't, what each piece costs in time, and where we think the risk sits.",
  },
];
---

<section class="v2-section" aria-labelledby="v2-scoping-title">
  <div class="v2-container v2-split">
    <div class="v2-split-sticky">
      <h2 class="v2-h2" id="v2-scoping-title">Two weeks of questions, then a written scope.</h2>
      <p class="v2-lede">We learn what you need, ask the right questions, and turn it into a clear plan.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="v2-scoping">
      <div class="v2-weeks">
        {
          weeks.map((week, i) => (
            <div class="v2-week" data-v2-reveal data-v2-delay={i * 120}>
              <span class="v2-week-n">{week.n}</span>
              <h3 class="v2-week-name">{week.name}</h3>
              <p class="v2-week-body">{week.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="v2-card v2-output" data-v2-reveal data-v2-delay={240}>
        <p class="v2-output-eyebrow">What you get</p>
        <p class="v2-output-body">
          A written scope: the feature list, what's deliberately excluded, a
          build order, a time estimate against each piece, and the questions
          still open. It's yours to hand to us, another studio, or a
          developer you already have.
        </p>
        <a class="v2-output-link v2-focus" href={site.booking} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          Book a scoping call <span class="v2-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .v2-scoping {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .v2-weeks {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .v2-weeks {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .v2-week {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--v2-border);
    border-radius: var(--v2-radius-card);
    background: var(--v2-card);
  }

  .v2-week-n {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--v2-muted);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .v2-week-name {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .v2-week-body {
    color: var(--v2-secondary);
    font-size: var(--v2-text-small);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .v2-output {
    padding: 32px;
  }

  .v2-output-eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--v2-text-eyebrow);
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--v2-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .v2-output-body {
    max-width: 56ch;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .v2-output-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: var(--v2-text-small);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--v2-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v2-border);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .v2-output-link .v2-arrow {
    transition: transform var(--v2-dur-micro) var(--v2-ease);
  }

  .v2-output-link:hover .v2-arrow {
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }
</style>
